  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2022-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let the given positive expression be \\(E.\\) Squaring it and using \\(1-\\frac{1}{p^2}=(1-\\frac{1}{p})(1+\\frac{1}{p})\\) gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} E^2&=\\prod_{p\\in\\{3,5,7\\}}\\frac{1+\\frac{1}{p}}{1-\\frac{1}{p}}\\\\ &=\\frac42\\cdot\\frac64\\cdot\\frac86=4. \\end{aligned} \\] Hence \\(E=2.\\)\n\nThus, the answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite each square-root factor as a product of two nearby fractions",
        "Pair each factor in the numerator with the matching factor under the square root"
      ],
